<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71563" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεν-όω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεινόω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξένος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make one's
				friend and guest, entertain,</i> in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξενοῦμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					927
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.849
			</span></i> : fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξενώσεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					92
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> mostly in 
				Pass.
			, with fut.
			
				Med.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξενώσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					303
				</span></i>
			 : pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξένωμαι</span> : aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξενώθην</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξενώθησαν Ἀττικῶς: ἐξενίσθησαν Ἑλληνικῶς</span>
				Moer.<i><span class="en">
				p.167
			</span></i> P.): </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>enter into a treaty of hospitality with</i> one, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλιες ἀλλήλῃσι ἐξεινώθησαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.21
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				642e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Ages.</u>
				8.5
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλεῦσιν ἐξενωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					6.48
				</span></i>
			 : abs., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.1.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>take up</i> one's <i>abode with</i> one <i>as a guest, to be
				entertained,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θήβᾳ ξενωθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.299
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				702
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i> l. c., etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξενωθεὶς τοῖσδ᾽ ἐν . . δόμοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξενοῦται τῷ Ξενοφῶντι, [παρ᾽]
				Ἑλλάδι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.8.6
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξενωθεὶς ὑπὸ τᾶς βουλᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(1).383
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Rhodes</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>reside abroad,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαρὸν ἐξενωμένου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					65
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				820
			</span></i> ; <i>go into banishment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				1085
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> later, in 
				Act.
			, <i>deprive</i> one <i>of</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[τινά] τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					6.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
